<title>UK: HK stocks in London closed after HK market holiday.</title>
<headline>HK stocks in London closed after HK market holiday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong stocks in London were closed for trade on Wednesday following a public and market holiday in Hong Kong marking China's resumption of sovereignty over the former British territory.</p>
<p>Dealers said Hong Kong stocks were expected to resume trading on the London Stock Exchange's SEAQ International on Thursday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496 (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
